; anumana: inference — knowing what is not directly seen from what is seen.
; one of the classical pramanas alongside pratyaksha (direct perception).
;
; the system uses anumana when:
; "a cat is an animal. there are 5 cats. how many animals?"
; → infer animal-count from cat-count via swarupa chain.
;
; structurally: walk swarupa edges to reach what is asked about
; from what is given. the inference is the walk itself.

(sangati anumana
  (swarupa pramana)
  (sthita pramana-sthalam)
  (kriya viveka)
  (janya pratyaksha)
  (phala satya)
  (abheda nyaya)
  (siddha parampara))
